---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SectionHeader from "@/components/SectionHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="CV" description="A concise CV for Jihwan Park focused on reliable cloud-native systems, air-gapped Kubernetes/K3S platforms, stateful service recovery, and resource-constrained systems work.">
  <section class="border-b border-white/10 py-12 lg:py-16">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500">CV</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold text-white md:text-5xl">Jihwan Park</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-base leading-8 text-slate-300 md:text-lg">
      Systems-first engineer interested in reliable cloud-native systems for constrained environments.
      My work connects air-gapped Kubernetes/K3S platforms, stateful service recovery, private artifact supply chains,
      degraded AI serving strategies, and resource-constrained AI systems.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-7 text-slate-400">
      I am not primarily focused on AI model design itself. My interest is in the systems infrastructure
      that allows internal services and AI workloads to run reliably under network, storage, hardware,
      and operational constraints.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm text-slate-300">
      <a class="rounded border border-white/15 px-3 py-2 hover:border-signal hover:text-signal" href="https://github.com/Petooooo">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12 lg:py-16">
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Interests" title="Research And Engineering Interests" description="The main direction is reliable infrastructure for internal services and AI workloads under operational constraints." />
    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      {[
        ["Reliable Cloud-Native Systems", "K3S, Kubernetes reliability, internal platforms, service exposure, GitOps-style workflows, and constrained deployment environments."],
        ["Air-Gapped Infrastructure", "Private registry, Nexus, image mirroring, bootstrap dependency paths, internal CI/CD, and artifact supply chains for restricted networks."],
        ["Storage / Stateful Recovery", "Longhorn-like PVC behavior, detach/attach delay, RTO/RPO-aware service design, and the practical boundary between hot failover and fault-tolerant recovery."],
        ["Operational AI Infrastructure", "Full-GPU workload constraints, degraded serving, inference service availability, traffic rerouting, and infrastructure around AI workloads rather than model architecture itself."]
      ].map(([title, body]) => (
        <div class="border-b border-white/10 py-4">
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">{title}</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">{body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-white/10 py-12 lg:py-16">
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Education" title="Education" description="A software and hardware background for systems work across the stack." />
    <div class="border-b border-white/10 py-4">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Kyung Hee University</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">B.E. in Computer Science and Engineering; double major in Electronic Engineering.</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">GPA: 4.26 / 4.5</p>
      <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-slate-500">2021 - 2025</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-white/10 py-12 lg:py-16">
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Experience" title="Selected Infrastructure Work" description="Publicly described at the level of constraints, architecture choices, and technical direction. Sensitive operational details are intentionally generalized." />
    <div class="grid gap-5">
      <div class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] p-5">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Air-Gapped K3S Internal Platform Migration</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-slate-500">2025 - Present</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">
          <li>Migrated Docker-only service operation toward a K3S-based internal cloud-native platform under restricted network conditions.</li>
          <li>Worked through service deployment standardization, internal image distribution, service exposure, persistent storage, and operational recovery concerns.</li>
          <li>Focused on practical service reliability in an environment where external registries, package repositories, public DNS, and managed cloud services were not freely available.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] p-5">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Stateful Workload Recovery with Longhorn</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-slate-500">2025 - Present</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">
          <li>Analyzed the operational gap between hot failover and fault-tolerant recovery when using Longhorn-backed PVCs for stateful services.</li>
          <li>Considered detach/attach delay, recovery time, service downtime, and RTO/RPO-aware design instead of overstating the system as fully zero-downtime.</li>
          <li>Used the experience to reason about which services can be statelessly rescheduled and which require storage-aware recovery planning.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] p-5">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Private Registry, Nexus, and Bootstrap Supply Chain</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-slate-500">2025 - Present</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">
          <li>Worked through private container registry, Nexus, image mirroring, and internal artifact distribution for air-gapped Kubernetes operation.</li>
          <li>Considered bootstrap dependency problems such as registry or Nexus self-dependency, where a failed artifact service must not depend only on itself for recovery.</li>
          <li>Investigated Maven/Nexus repository behavior, including how uploaded artifact paths can be governed by POM GAV metadata rather than only the chosen upload path.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] p-5">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Operationally Constrained AI Serving Strategy</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-slate-500">2025 - Present</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">
          <li>Evaluated GPU cluster operation for AI serving workloads where fine-grained GPU sharing was not always practical because production workloads required full-GPU allocation.</li>
          <li>Reasoned about degraded serving as a more realistic availability model: accepting lower capacity during failure while keeping the service alive.</li>
          <li>Compared the practical roles of MIG, time-slicing, full-GPU placement, active-active service replicas, and load-balancer-level traffic rerouting.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-white/10 py-12 lg:py-16">
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Projects" title="Selected Systems Projects" description="Graduation-level projects that connect lower-level resource constraints with AI workload execution." />
    <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
      {[
        [
          "Lifecycle-Aware Memory Analysis for TensorFlow Lite Micro",
          "TinyML runtime memory management project that analyzed tensor lifetimes, conflict relationships, BFS-style allocation ordering, and in-place update opportunities. Project evaluation reduced peak memory by 28.33% on Person Detect and 14.06% on Tiny U-Net compared with the original size-based allocation plan."
        ],
        [
          "Area-Efficient CNN Accelerator Using Bit-Shift Operations on Zynq FPGA",
          "Hardware-aware AI inference project using bit-shift operations, INQ/STE-based quantization, IM2COL, systolic array dataflow, and AXI4-Lite PS/PL integration. Project evaluation reported 36.5% FPGA area decrease and 8.83ms PS+PL runtime compared with 15.9ms PS-only execution."
        ]
      ].map(([title, body]) => (
        <div class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] p-5">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">{title}</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">{body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-white/10 py-12 lg:py-16">
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Skills" title="Technical Skills" description="Grouped by the systems layers that show up repeatedly in the work." />
    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      {[
        ["Systems / Infrastructure", "Linux, Docker, Kubernetes/K3S, Longhorn, private registry, Nexus, internal CI/CD, GitOps concepts, Traefik, NodePort/hostPort, TLS/HTTPS."],
        ["Data / Backend Systems", "MinIO, ClickHouse, MongoDB, RabbitMQ, asynchronous processing, SQL."],
        ["Programming", "C/C++, Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, Java, Go, SQL, Verilog."],
        ["Hardware / Embedded", "FPGA, Zynq, Vivado, Quartus, STM32, Arduino, Raspberry Pi."]
      ].map(([title, body]) => (
        <div class="border-b border-white/10 py-4">
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-slate-500">{title}</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">{body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-white/10 py-12 lg:py-16">
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Positioning" title="Working Identity" description="A concise summary of the direction I want to continue developing." />
    <div class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] p-5">
      <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-slate-300">
        I want to develop as a systems engineer and researcher who can reason across hardware,
        runtime, storage, networking, deployment, and service reliability. My strongest interests
        are not in building AI models themselves, but in designing the infrastructure that allows
        services and AI workloads to operate reliably in constrained, private, and operationally
        complex environments.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
